{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793488083,"nonce":"gz11vnmRsOSHIjDy6l9ULxQR/kY=","title":"A backend given its own promotion request never reaches it from a loop","message":"Since dd108e8b a loop's back-edge counter calls the preserving promotion request, and since e4d6bb59 that function is compiled once per process calling `osr::osr_request_promotion` directly. A backend made with `with_runtime_symbols` naming its own `__zyntax_osr_request` still has its loops call the process's request, so the function it supplied never runs.\n\nReproducer: `cargo test -p zyntax_compiler --test osr_tier_transfer only_a_running_hot_loop_requests_promotion`. It counts 0 requests where it expects 1. Rust CI 41249119612 failed it on x86_64 Linux, macOS and Windows; aarch64 is not in CI and the local runs did not include this test.\n\nProduction supplies no override (only the test does), so no runtime was affected; the loop calls still reached the real request.","files":null}]}